{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/MapReduce.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/MapReduce.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"map reduce map reduce","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/MapReduce.md","fileName":"MapReduce.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"MapReduce","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Scalable Social Data Processing]] [[.NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Scalable Social Data Processing",".NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns","bigdataincomplexandsocialnetworks.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/MapReduce.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/MapReduce.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"map reduce map reduce","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/MapReduce.md","fileName":"MapReduce.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"MapReduce","heading":"MapReduce","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"MapReduce is a distributed computation pattern that maps input partitions into intermediate records and reduces grouped records into results. Systems such as Pig and Hive can generate sequences of these jobs from higher-level transformations.\n\nThe model automates parallel work and data redistribution, but separate jobs impose overhead and typically reread intermediate state. Algorithms with repeated rounds therefore benefit from caching and long-running workers.\n\nWithin an in-process .NET example, map operations can be expressed as independent projections and the reduce phase as grouping and aggregation. That implementation demonstrates the decomposition, although it lacks the fault tolerance and data-placement machinery of a distributed MapReduce system.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Scalable Social Data Processing",".N